cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use the Explanation Integrity Benchmark (EIB), please cite the software entry below. Replace it with the paper
  once that is published -- see `preferred-citation`, which is filled in at submission.
title: "Explanation Integrity Benchmark (EIB): attribution rewriting attacks on intrusion detectors explained to machines"
abstract: >-
  A benchmark of prediction-preserving attacks on the post-hoc feature attributions that
  ML-based NIDS attach to their alerts, with per-instance detector-relative interventional
  labels, a realizable-flow constraint over the extractor's own arithmetic, and a downstream
  autonomous-consumer decision task. Ships the attacks, the integrity signals, the conformal
  calibration, and a one-command reproduction of every number in the paper.
type: software
